# Focus Grid v1.2 — Implementation Plan

## What Is Focus Grid?

Focus Grid is a **personal clarity tool** embedded within the myclass2026 project. The user arrives overwhelmed → dumps thoughts into a text box → AI sorts them into tasks vs. notes → user picks what matters today → opens a focused session → captures distractions without losing the thread → reviews at end of day.

**Core flow:** `DUMP → CLARIFY → PLAN → ACT → REVIEW`

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The original plan used **raw Vue 3 components**. This plan uses **Quasar 2** components (QTable, QCard, QDialog, QBtn, QInput, etc.) to match the existing myclass2026 codebase. The frontend also uses **Inertia.js** for page rendering and **Pinia** for state.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The plan includes an **AI venting feature** that calls an external AI API. Which AI provider should we use? The project already has `@google/generative-ai` and `openai` packages installed. We can use either — please confirm.

> [!WARNING]
> The offline-first sync (Phase 8) has been deferred to a later sprint. The database schema includes `version` and `sync_status` fields to prepare for it, but the frontend will operate online-first for v1.

## Frontend Location
All Quasar components and views will be stored under:
`resources/js/Pages/myclass2026/features/fg/`
Reusable components will go in `resources/js/Pages/myclass2026/features/fg/components/`.

